/-!
# Finite étale covers of a punctured hypersurface, and purity for the hypersurface

Let `(A, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring and `f ∈ 𝔪`.  Write `X = Spec A`, `X₀ = Spec (A / fA)`,
and let `U = X ∖ {𝔪}` and `U₀ = X₀ ∖ {𝔪}` be the two punctured spectra.  Assume

1. `A` is `f`-adically complete,
2. `f` is a nonzerodivisor,
3. `H¹_𝔪(A/fA)` and `H²_𝔪(A/fA)` are finite `A`-modules, and
4. purity holds for `(A_f)_𝔭` at every maximal ideal `𝔭 ⊂ A_f`.

Then the restriction functor `FÉt_U ⥤ FÉt_{U₀}` is essentially surjective; and if in addition
purity holds for `A`, then purity holds for `A / fA`.

Hypotheses (1)–(3) are exactly what makes the restriction functor
`colim_{U₀ ⊆ U' ⊆ U} FÉt_{U'} ⥤ FÉt_{U₀}` an equivalence, so a finite étale cover of `U₀` is
already defined over some open `U'` between `U₀` and `U`.  The points of `U` that `U'` omits are
maximal ideals of `A_f`, and hypothesis (4) extends the cover across them to a cover of `U`.
With purity for `A` the resulting cover of `U` extends over `X`, and the restriction of that
extension to `X₀` is the desired extension over `Spec (A / fA)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.exists_nbhd_finiteEtale_of_isAdicComplete` — under
  (1)–(3), every finite étale cover of `U₀` is the restriction of a finite étale cover of an open
  `U'` of `X` with `U₀ ⊆ U' ⊆ U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.essSurj_finiteEtaleBaseChange_U₀ToU_of_isAdicComplete`
  — under (1)–(4), the restriction functor `FÉt_U ⥤ FÉt_{U₀}` is essentially surjective.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.LocalLefschetzSituation.hasPurity_quotientRing_of_isAdicComplete` — under
  (1)–(4) together with purity for `A`, purity holds for `A / fA`.

## Implementation notes

The neighbourhoods of `U₀` in `U` come in two shapes.  The equivalence of the restriction functor
out of the colimit is proved for an ambient scheme with a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf, where a
neighbourhood is an open of the *ambient* scheme `U` containing the support of the sheaf; the
local Lefschetz situation instead indexes by the opens `U'` of `X` with `U₀ ⊆ U' ⊆ U`.  The two
are matched by pushing an open of `U` forward along `U ⟶ X`, which is the same scheme
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isoImage`), and by identifying `U₀` with the closed subscheme of
`U` cut out by the kernel of the closed immersion `U₀ ⟶ U`, which is generated by the restriction
of `f`.  Since both the ambient scheme and the ideal sheaf move when the open `U` is respelled as
the complement of the zero locus of `𝔪`, both are generalized in a private auxiliary statement so
that the two identifications can be substituted.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLF)
